            "exerciseNum": 3,
            "exerciseTitle": "Exercise 3: Complete the extract from an autobiography with th",
            "q": "Complete the extract from an autobiography with the correct form of the verbs from the box. be close   be devoted   bring up   care get on   look up to   spoil by take after   tell off   turn to My childhood wasn’t an ordinary one. When I was just a baby and my sister was two years old, our father got a new job which meant he had to spend long periods abroad. Because she had two young children, my mother decided to go back and live with her parents. As a result, my sister and I were _____________ partly by my mother’s parents, so that she could go out to work. My grandparents _____________ to us and did the best they could for us. We had a great relationship, but we certainly weren’t _____________ them and we were _____________ whenever we behaved badly. It was tough for my grandmother because as well as looking after us, she had to _____________ for her own mother, who was elderly at the time. My grandmother has often told me that I _____________ my mother, that I’m like her in so many ways, and that’s comforting to know. I was lucky in that I had a very good relationship with my sister. When I was growing up, I always _____________ her, admiring everything she did. _____________ to her to this very day. She feels the same and, in fact, she _____________ me before anyone else when she needs a second opinion on something or just wants to express her hopes and fears about things. It’s a lovely bond to have and it really _____________ my nerves when I hear people complaining about their brothers and sisters. Enjoy the time you have together, I say! B2   Unit test 12A: (1) Complete the sentence or answer the question.",
