            "question": "Choose the best option a–d to complete the text. If you’re like me, you may well have needed to someone to explain   certain technology to you at some point. Recently, much _____ about the speed with which technology changes, and the impact that by people as a result. Take the smartphone as an example. It seems that just as we’ve become used to _____ latest model, a new and improved one is waiting to take its place. This can leave many of us that we’re missing out on something if we don’t have it. And indeed _____ of us rush out to the shops, it seems, _____ time a new model appears, simply because we are not willing _____. But we should ask ourselves if a phone that’s only a year old really doesn’t have _____ features to keep us happy? _____ about consumer behaviour from this current trend. For one thing, it tells us that people are happy to stop _____ older models and just replace them with something new, whereas older generations kept something until it eventually broke and died! EXAMPLE : a   get someone to explain b   have someone to explain c   got someone to explain d   had someone to explain a   will be written b   has been written c   had been written d   will have been written a   could have been felt b   will be felt c   is felt d   should be felt b   an c   the a   feeling b   to feel c   feel d   is feeling a   much b   many c   both d   all a   either b   neither c   some d   each a   waiting b   wait c   not waiting d   to wait a   enough b   too many c   all d   lots of a   will be learned b   had been learned c   can be learned d   might have been learned a   to use b   using c   use d   having used B2   Progress test 2A Units 4–6: (10) Complete the sentence or answer the question.",
