            "q": "Complete the text with a suitable word. Write one word in each gap. Contractions (e.g.   I’m ) count as one word. When I was in my teens, my parents wanted to __________ what I wanted to be when I grew up. And when I informed __________ that I wanted to be an author, they __________ me they would do whatever it took to make sure my dreams came true, and encouraged me __________ follow my dream. I studied English at university and one day my studies advisor, who knew about my dream, suggested __________ a talk by a young author who was visiting the university. Her story was inspiring. The best piece of advice she gave us was this: ‘If I __________ you, I wouldn’t try to be too ambitious the first time round. Start small and see what happens. And remember, if you don’t try, you __________ know what the possibilities are.’ And she was right. __________ people try to make their dreams come true, they’ll never know what might have been. Right now, I’m about to have my first novel published, __________ soon as it is, I’ll send my studies advisor a signed copy. Sadly, my parents aren’t here to enjoy my success. If __________ they could see me, I’m sure they’d feel so proud.: (1) Complete the sentence or answer the question.",
