            "exerciseTitle": "Exercise 8: Read the article and underline five reference word",
            "q": "Read the article and underline five reference words used to refer back to earlier parts of the Poland, a country in eastern Europe, still shares some traditions with its Slavic and Scandinavian neighbours which seem to have some roots in old pagan traditions. The best example of these is probably Kupa ł a Night, which is celebrated on the shortest night of the year, generally the night of 21/22 June. The night is dedicated to the elements of fire and water, the moon, the sun, and love. While the origins of the name are unclear, it is thought to have come from either the Russian word to ‘bathe’, or possibly the Indo-European word kump   meaning ‘group’ or ‘community’. Whatever the origins, many younger people take the opportunity to celebrate by organizing bonfires. They also dance and have parties into the night. One tradition sees people jumping over flames to cleanse and protect themselves against evil and bad fortune. The most famous part of the evening, however, is when young women go down to the river and set wreaths of flowers decorated with candles afloat. According to the tradition, if the wreath is picked out by an unmarried man, marriage will soon take place. B2   Unit test 9A: (4) Complete the sentence or answer the question.",
